<% content_for :title, "Life: sleep, habits, tasks and screen time in one place" %>
<% content_for :description, "Life brings sleep, Apple Watch, iPhone screen time, tasks, habits and lab results together in one place. Free." %>
<div class="space-y-16">
  <%# Topo %>
  <header class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
    <%= link_to root_path, class: "flex items-center gap-2" do %>
      <%= image_tag "/images/landing/icon.png", alt: "", class: "h-9 w-9" %>
      <span class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Life</span>
    <% end %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <div class="hidden items-center overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white text-xs sm:flex">
        <% I18n.available_locales.each do |loc| %>
          <%= link_to locale_label(loc), locale_switch_path(loc),
                class: "px-2 py-1 #{I18n.locale == loc ? 'bg-emerald-50 font-semibold text-emerald-700' : 'text-slate-500 hover:bg-slate-50'}" %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <%= link_to "Sign in", new_user_session_path, class: "rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-600 hover:bg-slate-100" %>
      <%= link_to "Create a free account", new_user_registration_path, class: "rounded-lg bg-emerald-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-emerald-700" %>
    </div>
  </header>

  <%# Apresentação %>
  <section class="grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div>
      <p class="mb-3 inline-flex rounded-full bg-emerald-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-700">Free for everyone who joins now</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">How your day went, in one place.</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-600">Life brings together your sleep, Apple Watch activity, iPhone screen time, tasks, habits and lab results. And it lets you connect an AI assistant to understand what shapes your routine.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <%= link_to "Create a free account", new_user_registration_path, class: "rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-emerald-700" %>
        <% if @store[:ios_app_store_url].present? %>
          <%= link_to "Download on the App Store", @store[:ios_app_store_url], class: "rounded-xl bg-slate-900 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-slate-800" %>
        <% else %>
          <span class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-500">iPhone app: coming soon to the App Store</span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Works in the browser, on iPhone and on Mac. Already have an account? <%= link_to "Sign in", new_user_session_path, class: "font-medium text-emerald-700 hover:underline" %></p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex justify-center">
      <%= image_tag "/images/landing/01-hoje.png", alt: "Life Today screen on iPhone: sleep, activity, screen time and habits", class: "w-64 sm:w-72", fetchpriority: "high" %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# O que tem %>
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">What Life does</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <% [
        ["Today at a glance", "Last night with sleep stages, the day's rings, steps, resting heart rate, heart rate variability and screen time, on a single screen."],
        ["iPhone and Apple Watch health", "With your permission, it reads sleep, activity, heart, breathing, workouts, weight, mobility, hearing and nutrition from the Health app. It only reads: it never writes to Health."],
        ["Real screen time", "Usage per app and per hour of the day, weekly average and your busiest day, sent by Life for Mac or by an iPhone Shortcut."],
        ["Habits that check themselves", "Create habits tied to a metric, such as \"screen under 3 hours\" or \"30 minutes of exercise\", and Life marks the day when you hit the goal."],
        ["Task boards", "Boards with columns, due dates, comments and the history of each task."],
        ["Lab results and weight", "Record lab results and your weight, and follow how they change over time."],
      ].each do |title, text| %>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900"><%= title %></h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600"><%= text %></p>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 p-5 shadow-sm sm:col-span-2 lg:col-span-3">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Your AI assistant, with your data</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Connect Claude, ChatGPT or another MCP-compatible assistant. It reads and cross-references your data to answer questions like "does my phone before bed hurt my sleep?". You authorize it, choose whether it only reads or can also create tasks, and revoke it whenever you want.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# Telas %>
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Inside the app</h2>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Screens with sample data.</p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex snap-x gap-4 overflow-x-auto pb-4">
      <% [["01-hoje", "Today"], ["03-saude", "Health"], ["04-tempo-de-tela", "Screen time"], ["02-tarefas", "Tasks"], ["05-conta", "Account and privacy"]].each do |file, label| %>
        <figure class="w-48 shrink-0 snap-start sm:w-56">
          <%= image_tag "/images/landing/#{file}.png", alt: "Life #{label} screen on iPhone", class: "w-full", loading: "lazy" %>
          <figcaption class="mt-1 text-center text-xs text-slate-500"><%= label %></figcaption>
        </figure>
      <% end %>
      <figure class="w-64 shrink-0 snap-start self-center sm:w-72">
        <%= image_tag "/images/mac/mac-menu.png", alt: "Life for Mac in the menu bar", class: "w-full", loading: "lazy" %>
        <figcaption class="mt-1 text-center text-xs text-slate-500"><%= link_to "Life for Mac", mac_app_path, class: "hover:underline" %></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# How the data arrives %>
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">How the data arrives</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">iPhone app</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Reads iPhone and Apple Watch health, sends it to Life and shows the daily summary.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Life for Mac or a Shortcut</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">The iPhone does not let apps read screen time. <%= link_to "Life for Mac", mac_app_path, class: "font-medium text-emerald-700 hover:underline" %> sends the copy the Mac receives through iCloud. Without a Mac, an iOS 26 Shortcut sends the daily summary.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Browser</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">The full dashboard, habits, tasks and lab results, on any computer or phone.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# Strengths and limitations %>
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Strengths and limitations</h2>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">So you can decide whether Life is right for you.</p>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-emerald-700">What Life does well</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
          <li>Brings together data that is usually scattered: Health app, Apple Watch, Screen Time, tasks and lab results.</li>
          <li>Automatic habits: the day is checked from your data, with nothing to log.</li>
          <li>Screen time per hour of the day, which the iPhone itself does not export.</li>
          <li>An AI assistant can cross-reference everything, only with your authorization.</li>
          <li>Your data is never sold or used for advertising.</li>
          <li>You can delete your account and all data whenever you want, in the app or on the website.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-amber-700">What it does not do yet</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
          <li>iPhone only: there is no Android version yet.</li>
          <li>Screen time needs a Mac or an iPhone on iOS 26, and arrives hours late, after the day ends.</li>
          <li>Through the Mac, website and CarPlay usage are not included. Through the Shortcut, there is no per-hour detail.</li>
          <li>Health comes only from the Health app: other watches and bands need to sync with it first.</li>
          <li>It is not a medical device and gives no diagnosis or medical advice.</li>
          <li>It is a new product, made by an independent developer.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# Preço %>
  <section class="rounded-3xl bg-slate-900 p-8 text-white">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Pricing</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold">Free</p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-slate-300">For now, Life is free for everyone who joins. And everything that exists today will never be charged for: if a paid plan ever comes, it will only cover new features.</p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-400">That includes the daily summary, iPhone and Apple Watch health, screen time, automatic habits, tasks, lab results, weight, the AI assistant, the iPhone app and Life for Mac.</p>
    <%= link_to "Create a free account", new_user_registration_path, class: "mt-6 inline-flex rounded-xl bg-emerald-500 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-emerald-400" %>
  </section>

  <%# Rodapé %>
  <footer class="flex flex-col items-center gap-3 border-t border-slate-200 pt-6 text-xs text-slate-500">
    <nav class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1">
      <%= link_to "Life for Mac", mac_app_path, class: "hover:underline" %>
      <%= link_to t("pages.privacy_title"), privacy_path, class: "hover:underline" %>
      <%= link_to t("pages.terms_title"), terms_path, class: "hover:underline" %>
      <%= link_to t("pages.support_title"), support_path, class: "hover:underline" %>
    </nav>
    <p>Life is a product by <%= link_to "Integrattor", "https://integrattor.com.br", class: "hover:underline" %>.</p>
  </footer>
</div>
